Subject: dtlogin won't start after install
Date: 1998/08/03
Message-ID: <6q5a7d$of7$1@jetsam.uits.indiana.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 377609330
Organization: Indiana University, Bloomington
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.osf.misc

Hi DUNIX gurus,

I did a complete reinstall with Dunix version 4.0.  Now when the system boots
the following happens:

After the screen says "Starting Desktop Logon Display" the screen flashes
white and then black for approx. 10-15 minutes.  Then I get the message "The
x-server cannot be started on display :0..." "Suspending Desktop Login".

After this mess I can logon without the GUI's but the screen behaves unreliably.
We have an Apple Multi-Sync monitor attached to this machine.  It is the same
monitor that we have always had.  I did not have any problems before this
system install.

What gives?

Anurag



